<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Entitlements for the hardened runtime, which Developer ID distribution requires and which
    notarization checks.

    Deliberately short. Every entitlement is a thing the app is allowed to do that it could not
    otherwise, so the list is the answer to "what does trusting this actually grant", and it should
    stay readable in one screen.

    Not here, on purpose:
      - App Sandbox. This is direct Developer ID distribution, not the App Store. Adding the
        sandbox without also adding network-client, file-access and device entitlements would break
        the app quietly; adding all of them would grant more than this list does. When the menu-bar
        shell arrives and the App Store becomes a question, that is the moment to sandbox properly.
      - allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory / disable-library-validation. Nothing here
        generates code or loads third-party plug-ins, and each of those measurably weakens the
        hardened runtime.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- The microphone. Saathi is a companion you talk to; this is the whole premise. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
